  "description": "meme-id: she_said_girls_run_the_world; hasOverallIntent: mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two men walking and laughing, with overlaid text that reads: 'she said girls run the world... so i told her get back in the kitchen.' This text directly invokes a misogynistic stereotype that reduces women's roles to domestic labor, implying that women are only suited for the kitchen and not for positions of power or influence in society. The visual of two men enjoying themselves reinforces the idea that men are the ones who 'correct' or 'reclaim' societal roles for women, which is a common trope in misogynistic humor. The meme uses juxtaposition to map the idea of women being 'in charge' onto the absurd and demeaning notion of women being confined to the kitchen, thereby perpetuating harmful gender norms. The intent is to mock and belittle women's capabilities and societal roles, which falls under the category of misogynous content.",
